down. Uniting the opposition for a common cause, leaders stress the urgency to restore trust in the electoral process. At a rally in Delhi, they highlighted the importance of safeguarding voting rights against authoritarian measures.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gyanesh-kumar-can-no-longer-remain-in-his-position-tmcs-sagarika-ghose-demands-cecs-removal/articleshow/135421182.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gyanesh-kumar-can-no-longer-remain-in-his-position-tmcs-sagarika-ghose-demands-cecs-removal/articleshow/135421182.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-01T13:28:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135421394,imgsize-122599.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['PM Modi, Amit Shah suffering loss': Sanjay Raut on business concerns of traders ahead of INDIA bloc rally]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-amit-shah-suffering-loss-sanjay-raut-on-business-concerns-of-traders-ahead-of-india-bloc-rally/articleshow/135420587.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135420587.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sanjay Raut asserted that the rally by the INDIA bloc in Delhi would not disrupt business activities. He emphasized that this event signifies the people's demand for a change in government. Supporters of various political parties began gathering for the rally, which aims to address alleged voter roll tampering. The demonstration is expected to attract significant participation amid security measures by the police.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-amit-shah-suffering-loss-sanjay-raut-on-business-concerns-of-traders-ahead-of-india-bloc-rally/articleshow/135420587.cms]]></link><guid><!